         <title><![CDATA[Trump to swap some tariffs on Canadian goods amid midterm pressure]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/trump-susan-collins-tariffs-midterms-9.7393675?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/176bbcfe-f8d7-43b2-8105-7563b3efb1c0,1792780678029/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C239%2C7600%2C4275%29%3B' alt='U.S. President Donald Trump walks on the South Lawn as he departs the White House on October 12, 2026 in Washington, DC.' width='620' height='349' title='U.S. President Donald Trump walks on the South Lawn as he departs the White House on October 12, 2026 in Washington, DC.'/><p>U.S. President Donald Trump is poised to lift tariffs on some Canadian products — and hit others with new duties — as Republicans in border states lobby for relief from trade actions that have put them in a shaky political position ahead of November's midterms.</p>]]></description>
